  "summary": "作者释武破昌曲合会命身带来才智技艺及奔波起伏，同时修正古赋单凭庙陷断富贫的说法：须合会吉会煞与行限，武破亥命会多吉也未必不遂，旺宫会多煞也未必富。四星合会命身不等于全部同宫，相关赋文为章节回指而非新增命例。",
  "summary_en": "The author reads Wu Qu, Po Jun, Wen Chang and Wen Qu meeting Life and Body as intelligence, technical aptitude and an unsettled life, but rejects judging wealth or failure by brightness alone. Benefic and malefic support and timing matter: even Wu Qu–Po Jun at Hai may fare well with benefics, while a strong palace with many malefics may not bring wealth. Meeting across Life and Body does not mean all four stars are co-located. The quoted related verses are cross-references, not new case placements.",
